  "source_corrections": [
    "Pinned maintained MIT Avocado implementation establishes two-dimensional Matern32 time/wavelength GP and dedicated astronomical augmentation and features, not generic flux correction plus tsfresh/cesium.",
    "Weighted grouped LightGBM folds replace unsupported MLP ensemble and Platt-calibration intake claims.",
    "Known/unknown probability adjustment uses explicit galactic/extragalactic masks and task-tuned unknown-class formula, not general novelty detection.",
    "Current LightGBM callbacks and instance RandomState are adaptations; no identical historical submission or predictive accuracy claim."
  ],
  "reuse_work": [
    "Separate generic numeric GP, feature reduction, weighted multiclass learning and probability normalization from astronomical wavelength/redshift and class-mask policies.",
    "Inspect registered numeric alternatives before adding providers and retain exact source behavior and licenses.",
    "Expose augmentation, feature construction, fold allocation and weighted fitting as explicit stages; do not retain only opaque prepare/train/predict selection.",
    "Validate full configured augmentation and fold lifecycle, both weighting modes and final known/unknown probabilities before stored original promotion.",
    "Bound native pools and LightGBM n_jobs explicitly for every validation run; the retained runtime permits caller-defined worker counts."
  ],
